{"ts": "2026-11-19T07:42:12.407304Z", "run_id": "r-20261119T0738Z-d381", "unit": "openspec:restyle-web-kit", "seq": 12, "type": "delegate.result", "question": "Q-006", "id": "Q-006", "status": "answered", "reason": "The generated end-to-end test failed at both base and head, so its head failure is not evidence against the code. The unit's own browser test traces the criterion with the exact assertions of the scenario and passed in the e2e gate (2617 of 2617 tests passed, e2e gate pass). I checked data.css, tokens.css, DataTable.tsx, the admin table spec and app.css: every asserted colour, radius, weight, overflow and caption value follows from the rules and tokens, and no other stylesheet overrides them.", "called": true, "tasks": [], "target": "H-5c5d8c36", "kind": "verdict", "batch": "Q-006+5", "batch_size": 5, "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code", "cost_usd": 0.555345, "decision": "accept", "answer_sha256": "905524a67eccc8c372c01430ace9149bf02f461135c7b85ea28e717469279617", "checked": [{"ref": "web/src/kit/data/data.css:5", "quote": ".ui-table-wrap {", "claim": "The wrapper rule is the card: it carries overflow-x auto, the divider border and the large radius in the following lines."}, {"ref": "web/src/kit/data/data.css:7", "quote": "border: 1px solid var(--ui-color-divider);", "claim": "The wrapper border uses the divider token."}, {"ref": "web/src/kit/data/data.css:8", "quote": "border-radius: var(--ui-radius-lg);", "claim": "The wrapper radius uses the large radius token."}, {"ref": "web/src/kit/data/data.css:25", "quote": ".ui-table thead th {", "claim": "The header cell rule sets the surface background and weight 600 on the following lines."}, {"ref": "web/src/kit/data/data.css:27", "quote": "background: var(--ui-color-surface);", "claim": "The header cell background is the surface token."}, {"ref": "web/src/kit/data/data.css:13", "quote": ".ui-table-caption {", "claim": "The caption rule exists and sets font-weight 600 two lines below."}, {"ref": "web/src/kit/data/data.css:42", "quote": ".ui-table tbody tr:hover {", "claim": "The hover row rule exists."}, {"ref": "web/src/kit/data/data.css:43", "quote": "background: var(--ui-color-accent-surface);", "claim": "The hovered row is the accent surface token."}, {"ref": "web/src/kit/tokens.css:26", "quote": "--ui-color-divider: #d0d5dd;", "claim": "The divider token resolves to rgb(208, 213, 221)."}, {"ref": "web/src/kit/tokens.css:24", "quote": "--ui-color-accent-surface: #eff4ff;", "claim": "The accent surface token resolves to rgb(239, 244, 255)."}, {"ref": "web/src/kit/tokens.css:3", "quote": "--ui-color-surface: #f4f5f7;", "claim": "The surface token resolves to rgb(244, 245, 247)."}, {"ref": "web/src/kit/tokens.css:38", "quote": "--ui-radius-lg: 0.5rem;", "claim": "The large radius is 8px at the default root font size."}, {"ref": "web/src/kit/data/DataTable.tsx:59", "quote": "<div className=\"ui-table-wrap\" role=\"region\" aria-label={model.caption} tabIndex={0}>", "claim": "The table sits in the card wrapper, which the test reads with closest."}, {"ref": "web/src/kit/data/DataTable.tsx:61", "quote": "<caption className={captionClass(props.captionDisplay)}>{model.caption}</caption>", "claim": "The caption carries the caption class and the caption text."}, {"ref": "web/src/kit/data/data-table.ts:206", "quote": "return display === \"hidden\" ? \"ui-table-caption ui-visually-hidden\" : \"ui-table-caption\";", "claim": "The caption class list always contains ui-table-caption."}, {"ref": "web/src/admin/pages.ts:50", "quote": "caption: \"Users\",", "claim": "The Users page table caption is Users."}, {"ref": "web/src/styles/app.css:4", "quote": "@import \"../kit/data/data.css\" layer(components);", "claim": "The data stylesheet is loaded in the components layer of the app."}, {"ref": "e2e/test_m6b_kit.py:114", "quote": "assert wrap == [\"rgb(208, 213, 221)\", \"8px\", \"auto\"]", "claim": "The repository's browser test asserts the scenario's wrapper values."}, {"ref": "e2e/test_m6b_kit.py:129", "quote": "assert row.evaluate(background) == \"rgb(239, 244, 255)\"", "claim": "The repository's browser test asserts the hover colour of the Bob Example row."}, {"ref": "test:test_m6b_kit::test_users_table_is_a_card_with_a_header_and_a_hover_row[chromium]", "quote": "test_users_table_is_a_card_with_a_header_and_a_hover_row", "claim": "The unit's own browser test of this scenario passed in the latest e2e gate run."}]}
